# Measured evidence seat — round 7 — working notes

Build: commit 984a0f17, frozen. Driving the wrapped copy _gate-suite.html.
Method: read source (src/*.css, src/*.js), then drive in chromium via playwright,
probing computed styles / a11y tree / focus order / repaint effects.

## Log

- Ran audit.mjs myself: exit 1 with contrast 21 / tracking 10 / spaceLadder 302.
  Contrast sightings are all `1:1 (needs 4.5)` on notes.voice + notes.seam, i.e. the
  model reads fg==bg. Screenshotted notes.voice at 1920: the dictation floor is a full
  opaque ink overlay; the flagged nodes are the sheet BEHIND it. Model error, not a
  render defect. NOT a finding.
- notes.voice focus trap is correct: Tab cycles exactly Cancel / Stop and read it back,
  never reaching the occluded sheet. Clean.

### FINDING 1 (headline) — Enter during a keyboard carry leaves the board mutated,
### stuck in the picked-up state, and with no undo.
src/tasks.js onKey: the Space branch (≈l.2924-2969) is the ONLY drop path. The
`if (key === "Enter")` branch (≈l.2971-2991) calls openCard(id, ...) with no
`carriedId` guard. Driven at 1440, tasks.board:
  Space on demo-t-01  -> aria-grabbed=true, data-force=moving, lane todo
  ArrowRight          -> lane DOING (carryMove already called moveTo(), the model
                         is mutated), say "In progress, position 1 of 4."
  Enter               -> "Task open.", focus to ASIDE.taskPanel
  Escape              -> "Task closed.", focus back on the card
  Ctrl+Z              -> "NOTHING LEFT TO UNDO."   (arm() never ran)
  Ctrl+Z again        -> same
After all that the card is permanently in In progress, still carries
aria-grabbed="true" and data-force="moving" (2px indigo outline + 1.5px indigo
ring + 5px halo + scale(1.02) + lift — the loudest treatment on the board),
with document.activeElement === BODY. Screenshot _zz-stuck-moving.png confirms.
Escape during a carry cancels correctly and clears both attributes; only Enter
leaks. Round 6's "the keyboard drop arms one" fix covered the Space drop only.

WIDER THAN ENTER. Same probe, other exits from a live carry (all at 1440,
tasks.board, card demo-t-01 walked one lane right so the model is already
mutated):
  Tab            -> lane doing, aria-grabbed=true, data-force=moving, Ctrl+Z
                    "Nothing left to undo."
  rail Notes/back-> lane doing, aria-grabbed=true, data-force=moving, Ctrl+Z
                    "Nothing left to undo."
  click empty lane ground -> endCarry() DOES run, attributes clear, says
                    "…put down in the in progress column." and Ctrl+Z STILL
                    says "Nothing left to undo."
So Space is the only exit that arms an undo (src/tasks.js l.2955 arm({kind:"move"…}))
and Escape (l.2883) the only exit that reverts. endCarry() (l.2639) commits the
lane change and never calls arm().
CODE/COMMENT DISAGREEMENT: the comment above endCarry() (l.2632-2638) states the
class was fixed — "Tab away, complete another card with the pointer, open the
composer or the Planning drawer, and the carry ran on". endCarry() is wired to
pointerdown only (l.4442). Tab away still runs the carry on, exactly as the
comment says it used to.

### Things I tried to break and could not (recording so the panel knows what was tested)
- Suite persistence: typed a 45-char draft in .topField, scrolled .index to 260,
  switched Notes -> Tasks -> Timeline -> Notes. Draft identical, index scrollTop
  still 260. The suite's central claim holds.
- Rover reach in tasks.dense: exhaustive up/down/right traversal reaches all 32
  visible cards. No unreachable card.
- Roving tabindex is consistent across all four surveyed states (one stop per
  group, -1 on the rest); the rail's arrow walk reaches the account tile at
  position 6.
- notes.voice focus trap: 28 tabs cycle exactly two controls.
- Space on .tick (role=checkbox) ticks; it does NOT pick the card up
  (src/tasks.js l.2916 guards it). Contract key intact.
- .idxRow hover is alive (my first sweep hit row 0, which is [data-cursor] and
  already carries --wash — false positive, withdrawn).

### FINDING 2 — every Tasks lane becomes a 13–44px sideways scroller between
### 1199 and ~1420, and one trackpad gesture slides the cards out of register.
Mechanism: src/tasks.css l.1053-1078. `.cardDots` grows a 24px mark into a 44px
target with `padding: 10px` + `margin: -13px -10px -13px auto` and
`box-sizing: content-box`. The negative right margin pulls the box back
VISUALLY, but negative margins do not shrink an ancestor's scrollable overflow,
and `.trayBody` is `overflow-x: auto`. Measured (tasks.dense, fresh page, no
interaction):
  .trayBody scrollWidth-clientWidth  @1440 [0,0,0,0,0]
                                     @1400 [3,4,0,0,0]
                                     @1360 [11,12,2,0,0]
                                     @1320 [19,20,10,0,0]
                                     @1280 [27,28,18,0,0]   <- declared viewport
                                     @1200 [43,44,34,0,0]   <- board floor is 1199
  tasks.board @1280 [13,14,4,0,0]; tasks.compact @1200 [11,12,0,0,0].
The offending descendant is .cardDots, right edge 23px past .trayBody's right
edge; the cards themselves sit 6px INSIDE it.
Reachable: one `mouse.wheel(80, 0)` over the To do lane at 1280 sets
scrollLeft 27/27. Screenshot _zz-ev-wheelshift.png: the whole To do column has
slid left, the first card's tick circle is sliced in half by the lane's left
edge, the ··· menu is exposed, and the column is now visibly out of register
with its own "TO DO 10" heading, which did not move.
No fade, no snap, nothing in the scrolled region — the guillotine edge from the
lessons file, at a width the console screenshots.
